Always use explicit mathematical calculations for all distances, widths, heights, paddings, and margins when positioning elements.
For coordinates and layout, apply direct mathematical reasoning—prefer formulas and expressions over hardcoded values.
Use geometric, geodesic, and linear math principles for all spatial computations and positioning logic.
Ensure all layout and positioning is derived from clear, maintainable mathematical relationships.